<title>UK: B.A.T slips after U.S. court ruling.</title>
<headline>B.A.T slips after U.S. court ruling.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1996-12-27</dateline>
<text>
<p>Shares in B.A.T Industries Plc were down 4p at 477-1/2p, against the stronger market trend, following news that a U.S. court had ruled a U.S. state could sue tobacco companies to recover money spent treating smoking related illnesses, market makers said on Friday.</p>
<p>&quot;News like this usually spooks tobacco stocks -- especially when volume is so thin,&quot; one market maker said.</p>
<p>A U.S. judge on Monday dismissed a lawsuit filed by four tobacco companies seeking to block the U.S. state of Connecticut's lawsuit, which also seeks to halt agressive marketing of tobacco products to children.</p>
<p>The tobacco companies involved in the case were Philip Morris, R.J. Reynolds, Lorillard Tobacco, and B.A.T's U.S. subsidiary, Brown &amp; Williamson.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7717</p>
